    description: "WHAT (owner ruling). The target is 60 s wall for a local smart-test run. It is REPORTED by each run and gates nothing. When a run misses it, the report names the largest parts: the analysis or graph walk, the number of selected tests and their test-seconds, the slowest single test. No CI target until CI's time before the first test is measured (the cadence item).\n\nUNITS. The replay counted test-seconds; this is wall time. On this machine smart-test uses up to 6 workers, capped by free memory.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. A real run that meets the target and one that misses it, each with the line it printed; a test for the report.\n\nSOURCE. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_plan_11152026.md; the owner's rulings of 2026-11-17 are its second 'Made' table. Measurements: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_followup_11172026/README.md, slice_graph_11152026/README.md, stale_graph_1a_11152026/README.md, fast_smart_test_11152026/README.md (the 37-PR replay)."  # 9bd8
